-- title:
--   Descent field K₀ as admissible small constants, q=3
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=3$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$. The geometric input consists of: a finite set $W$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places (rational, affine geometric, with $j$-value in the supersingular set), an inclusion $\mathrm{hle}$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ whose residue computes coefficientwise reduction of Laurent series over $A$, an element $\pi\in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$, an index $\zeta$ of primitive $q$-th roots of unity, and two families $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ (indexed by $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{Z}/q)$) and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ (indexed by $W$) of valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, subject to axioms summarised here: the membership description of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ by ratios of Laurent series over $A$ with denominator of nonzero reduction, transitivity of $\Gamma_0(M')$ on the Igusa family through $\mathrm{levelAutBar}$, injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$, permutation of the Igusa family under $\mathrm{levelAutBar}$, the identification of constants in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ with $A$, the compatibility of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ with $R_0$ and with residues of elements of $A$, invariance of each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ under $\mathrm{levelAutBar}$, and the existence in each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ of an element $t$ with $t-a$ a unit for every $a\in A$. The descent data consist of a subfield $K_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/K_0$ algebraic and $\pi\in K_0$; a henselian discrete valuation domain $A_0$ with an injective local ring homomorphism $\iota\colon A_0\to A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is $A\cap K_0$, such that $A_0\to\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ is surjective, with uniformiser $\varpi_0$ satisfying $\iota(\varpi_0)=\pi$; and a subfield $F_0$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ consisting of those elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $K_0$, containing the image of $\mathrm{jq}$, together with an $A_0$-algebra structure on $F_0$ whose structure map is $\iota$ followed by the inclusion of constants. The conclusion asserts the existence of an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and an element $\pi_0\in k_0$ lying in $A$ such that $k_0$ and $K_0$ have the same underlying set, $\pi_0=\pi$, and: $A\cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) is a henselian discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ and algebraically closed residue field; every element of $A$ differs from some element of $k_0\cap A$ by an element of the maximal ideal of $A$; there is a prime $\ell$ with $\ell\ge 3$, $\ell\neq q$, $\ell\nmid M'$ and a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity in $k_0$; $\pi_0^{q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$; and there is a ring isomorphism $A_0\simeq A\cap k_0$ compatible with $\iota$.
--
--   This is the $q=3$ case of the step verifying that the descent field $K_0$ furnishes an admissible field of small constants for the Igusa base model over $A$: it converts the abstract descent datum $(K_0,A_0,\iota,\varpi_0,F_0)$ into an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ whose intersection with $A$ is a henselian discrete valuation ring with the required uniformiser, roots of unity and residue field. It feeds the later constructions of the descended Igusa and Drinfeld rings and their formal smoothness statements.
